# Changelog

## 2026-11-07

- Training metrics now use invariant decimal parsing, failed iterations use capped exponential backoff, and the loop stops after the configured consecutive-failure limit. Concurrent TinyStories downloads use isolated temporary files.
- `IdleOnly` rechecks idle state before each iteration and during training, stops when activity resumes or idle detection becomes unavailable, and requests Task Scheduler idle-end stopping. Training process-tree cleanup has a 15-second grace period; if cleanup cannot be verified, the loop stops with exit code 3 and retains the worktree. Real Task Scheduler handling of supervisor descendants remains unverified; see the disposable VM procedure in `docs/idle-policy-disposable-vm.md`.

## 2026-11-06

- The launcher verifies the canonical checkout root, `main` branch, and single matching `origin` before update or launch. Scheduled-task runtime selection prefers PowerShell 7 and falls back to Windows PowerShell 5.1, refusing task changes if neither is available.
- Scheduled runs start cold; recovery requires an operator-selected compatible checkpoint and explicit `--resume-from`. Checkpoint cleanup applies 5-run and 30-day limits to completed compatible runs while preserving active, interrupted, malformed, unsupported, incompatible, and `recovery-needed` runs.
- Windows CI now runs locked, CPU-safe Python unittest discovery.

## 2026-11-03

- Timed-out training now uses process-tree cleanup and verification. If cleanup cannot be verified, the loop stops with a distinct exit code and retains the iteration worktree; idle-only scheduling also skips when Windows idle data cannot be validated.
- Checkpoints now record the dataset SHA-256 and tokenizer fingerprint. Resume validation rejects mismatched identities and older checkpoints without that metadata.
- CI and npm validation helpers are tracked, and `npm test` first checks local script references against a clean Git archive.

## 2026-11-01

- `-RunLoop` now requires a clean source checkout, serializes loops per repository, and runs each candidate in an isolated experiment worktree. Only `train.py` is staged there, and keep or discard decisions affect only the experiment branch.
- Model-generated training code now requires an interactive review and the exact `RUN REVIEWED TRAIN.PY` approval before training. Declined candidates remain available for review, and provider credentials are limited to the selected AI CLI and cleared before training.
- Large edit prompts now reach `ai-powered` through UTF-8 stdin, with temporary prompt cleanup after the invocation.

## 2026-09-10

- Launcher defaults now persist only non-secret operational settings under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\myTech.Today\autoresearch-win-rtx-scheduled\launch.json`, while the legacy `scripts\launch.json` path remains read for compatibility only.
- Scheduled task launches now use a first-class `-TaskSupervisor` flow that starts the hidden `-RunLoop` child, writes `autoresearch-task-launch.json`, and propagates the child exit code.
- Added `Unattended` scheduler policy support via S4U logon and exposed Task Scheduler history enablement in the launcher GUI.
- Run-log pruning now records a pruning plan before deletion and a completion summary after deletion.
- `train.py` now raises `OptimizerSetupError` when optimizer parameter grouping drifts, which keeps the invariant enforced even when Python optimization strips `assert` statements.
- Windows CI now uploads GUI layout PNG artifacts alongside JSONL and log files on failure.
